{"seeAlsoSections":[{"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides","identifiers":["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry is a list someone has to keep in step with the code: every analytics event type in an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"array, every route in a table, every dependency registered in one function at startup. A new type"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that isn’t added works everywhere except where the list is read, and nothing tells you. Moving the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"list onto LinkerSets takes four steps, and the list is deleted at the end."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Take an analytics library whose events are types conforming to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"AnalyticsEvent"},{"type":"text","text":", collected by"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hand so the library can validate their schemas at launch:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public protocol AnalyticsEvent {","    static var name: String { get }","}","","\/\/ Every module's events, listed by hand.","let allEvents: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] = [","    Login.self,","    Logout.self,","    PurchaseCompleted.self,","]"],"type":"codeListing"},{"level":3,"text":"1. Give the library a macro","anchor":"1-Give-the-library-a-macro","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick a kind (“evnt” is "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0x6576_6E74"},{"type":"text","text":", as "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" explains) and add a compiler plugin"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whose macro requires the protocol, so its records hold "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"any AnalyticsEvent.Type"},{"type":"text","text":":"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public enum EventMacro: LinkerSetMacro {","    public static func kind(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> UInt32 { 0x6576_6E74 }  \/\/ \"evnt\"","","    public static func requiredConformance(of attribute: AttributeSyntax) -> TypeSyntax? {","        \"Analytics.AnalyticsEvent\"","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The library declares the macro and the kind, re-exports LinkerSets for the expansion, and reads"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the set for its users:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@_exported import LinkerSets","","extension LinkerSetKind {","    static let events = LinkerSetKind(rawValue: 0x6576_6E74)  \/\/ \"evnt\"","}","","@attached(peer)","public macro Event() = #externalMacro(module: \"AnalyticsMacros\", type: \"EventMacro\")","","public enum AnalyticsEvents {","    public static var all: [any AnalyticsEvent.Type] {","        LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values","    }","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The re-export is required. The expansion lands in each user’s file and names","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"LinkerSets.LinkerSetRecord","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" there, so that file must see the LinkerSets module. A library that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"imports LinkerSets without re-exporting it leaves its users’ files failing with “cannot find","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"‘LinkerSets’ in scope” unless each one imports LinkerSets too. The re-export also puts","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSet","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetKind","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":" in scope wherever the library is imported. Keep the kind","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"internal and hand users the values through the library’s own API (","type":"text"},{"code":"AnalyticsEvents.all","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), so the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set is read in one place.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The LinkerSetsMacroSupport module’s documentation has the package targets this needs.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"2. Read the set beside the list","anchor":"2-Read-the-set-beside-the-list","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Before touching any event, read both and compare them, in a test or a debug build:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let discovered = AnalyticsEvents.all","let missing = allEvents.filter { listed in !discovered.contains { $0 == listed } }"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"missing","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" starts as the whole list and shrinks as events are marked."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"3. Mark each event where it’s declared","anchor":"3-Mark-each-event-where-its-declared","type":"heading"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["@Event","struct Login: AnalyticsEvent {","    static let name = \"login\"","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"An event that doesn’t conform fails to compile. A generic event type, or one nested in a generic"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"type, is refused with a message, as "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" lists; such a type needs its concrete"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"specializations listed by hand, or a concrete wrapper."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"4. Delete the list","anchor":"4-Delete-the-list","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"missing"},{"type":"text","text":" is empty, the library reads the set instead:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["let allEvents = LinkerSet<any AnalyticsEvent.Type>(kind: .events).values"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"and the hand-written array goes. A new event is registered by writing "},{"code":"@Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" on it, in whichever"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module declares it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"level":3,"text":"Other registries","anchor":"Other-registries","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The same steps fit any list whose entries can be declared as constants, functions or types:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Routes"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Route static let profile = Route(path: \"\/profile\")"},{"type":"text","text":", read as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<Route>"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Migrations"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":": ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@Migration static func addUsers(_ db: inout Database)"},{"text":", read as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"LinkerSet<(inout Database) -> Void>"},{"text":", sorted by a version the migration declares.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Dependency registrations"}]},{"type":"text","text":": "},{"code":"@Registration static func register(_ container: Container)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", each"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"module registering its own factories, read and called once at startup."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A registry whose order matters gets it from the entries, never from the set: the linker’s order is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"stable but not one you choose ("},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":")."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets"]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/ReplacingARegistry","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Move a central list of event types, routes or registrations onto declarations that find"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"themselves."}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/linkersets\/replacingaregistry"]}],"metadata":{"role":"article","modules":[{"name":"LinkerSets"}],"roleHeading":"Article","title":"Replacing a hand-written registry"},"kind":"article","sections":[],"references":{"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSetKind":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The tag that says which client a linker-set record belongs to.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSetKind","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSetKind","title":"LinkerSetKind","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkersetkind"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/DeclaringAKind":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Pick the number that tags your declarations, and decide whether your users write it."}],"title":"Declaring a kind","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/declaringakind","kind":"article","type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/DeclaringAKind","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/PlatformsAndLinking":{"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/platformsandlinking","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Where records are found, how, and which test shows it."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/PlatformsAndLinking","kind":"article","title":"Platforms and linking","role":"article"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets":{"abstract":[{"text":"Declarations that register themselves at compile time and are found at run time across every module a program links.","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets","kind":"symbol","role":"collection","title":"LinkerSets","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/LinkerSet":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every record of one kind, across every image the program has loaded, and the values they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"produce."}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"LinkerSet","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/LinkerSet","title":"LinkerSet","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/linkerset"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/FindingRecords":{"kind":"article","type":"topic","title":"Finding records","role":"article","identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/FindingRecords","abstract":[{"text":"Read every declaration of a kind, as the type you expect.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/findingrecords"},"doc://LinkerSets/documentation/LinkerSets/WhatTheMacrosRefuse":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Every declaration a record can’t describe is a compile error, with a message that says why."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/LinkerSets\/documentation\/LinkerSets\/WhatTheMacrosRefuse","kind":"article","role":"article","title":"What the macros refuse","url":"\/documentation\/linkersets\/whatthemacrosrefuse"}}}